config AKIRA_WASM_CRYPTO_ED25519
    bool "Export Ed25519 keygen/sign to WASM"
    default n
    depends on AKIRA_WASM_CRYPTO
    help
      Expose Ed25519 key generation and signing to WASM via a standalone
      RFC 8032 implementation on mbedtls_mpi + mbedtls_sha512 (this
      mbedTLS vendor drop has no twisted-edwards curve, so PSA can't do
      Ed25519 here — see src/api/ed25519.c).
      Capability: "crypto" (bit 28), same as AKIRA_WASM_CRYPTO.
      Without this, crypto_ed25519_keygen/sign always return -ENOTSUP.

config AKIRA_WASM_CRYPTO_ECDSA_P256
    bool "Export P-256/ECDSA keygen/sign to WASM"
    default n
    depends on AKIRA_WASM_CRYPTO
    select MBEDTLS_PSA_CRYPTO_C
    select PSA_WANT_ALG_ECDSA
    select PSA_WANT_ECC_SECP_R1_256
    select PSA_WANT_KEY_TYPE_ECC_KEY_PAIR_GENERATE
    select PSA_WANT_KEY_TYPE_ECC_KEY_PAIR_IMPORT
    select PSA_WANT_KEY_TYPE_ECC_KEY_PAIR_EXPORT
    select PSA_WANT_ALG_SHA_256
    help
      Expose P-256 (secp256r1) key generation and ECDSA/SHA-256 signing to
      WASM via PSA Crypto. Unlike Ed25519, this mbedTLS vendor drop DOES
      support P-256 (it's a Weierstrass curve), so this goes through PSA
      properly instead of a vendored implementation.
      Capability: "crypto" (bit 28), same as AKIRA_WASM_CRYPTO.
      Without this, crypto_p256_keygen/sign always return -ENOTSUP.
      Needed for U2F (FIDO U2F mandates P-256, no alternative curve).

